### Common Patterns

All three participants kept booking, changing/canceling, and appointment information together. They also all grouped office hours with walk-in availability, renewal with fees, and title replacement with ownership transfer. I plan to use these groupings as starting points on my proposed sitemap revision for grouped links. 

### Label and Grouping Differences

Participant A used service labels such as “Registration” and “Titles.” B used more action-oriented labels such as “Register or renew” and “Make an appointment.” C used broader labels such as “Manage vehicles” and “Go to the DMV.”

Participants A and C grouped appointment booking with office hours. B put office hours under “Get Help” and booking under “Make an appointment.” This suggests that some users may look for office information or specific section headings. 

### Unexpected Groupings

Participant C grouped out-of-state registration with ownership and title tasks. Participants A and B grouped it with registration and renewal. All three still placed out-of-state registration and new vehicle registration together. That supports giving both registration tasks clear labels while also adding a cross-link from the title and ownership section.

Mailing address updates also had no consistent group. A and B grouped that card with plates and placards, while C grouped it with registration renewal. A direct “Update mailing address” link, with an additional link from renewal, would give users more than one way to find it.
